
# 2. Doubly Linked List

## Question Description
Implement a Doubly Linked List in C++ using dynamic memory allocation. Each node contains data, a pointer to the previous node, and a pointer to the next node. Insert elements at the end and display the list.

## Test Cases

### Test Case 1
Input: `10, 20, 30`

Expected Output:
`10 <-> 20 <-> 30 <-> NULL`

### Test Case 2
Input: `5, 15`

Expected Output:
`5 <-> 15 <-> NULL`

### Test Case 3
Input: `7`

Expected Output:
`7 <-> NULL`

## Time Complexity
- Insert at end: O(n) per insertion
- Display: O(n)

## Space Complexity
- O(n)
